{
  "_comment": "Golden table for Damage.compute (SPEC-stats-status). Every expected value is hand-computed from the reference formula below so balance changes are explicit diffs (reviewed by both developers during the week-12 balance pass).",
  "reference_formula": "raw = hit.base_damage * (attacker.ATTACK / 100.0) * hit.ability_power_scale(attacker.ABILITY_POWER); crit = hit.force_crit or (host_rng.randf() < CRIT_CHANCE + hit.bonus_crit_chance); crit_mult = 1.5 + CRIT_DAMAGE if crit else 1.0; status_mult = 1.0 (StatusEffects terms land week 4); defense = max(target.DEFENSE, 0); mitigation = 100.0 / (100.0 + defense); final = round(raw * crit_mult * status_mult * hit.multiplier * mitigation), minimum 1 on a connecting hit",
  "ability_power_scale": "HitData.ability_power_scale(ap): 1.0 unless scales_with_ability_power, then max(1.0 + (ap - 100.0) / 100.0, 0.0). Choice recorded in .goals/LOG.md — the exact curve is HitInfo's (Dev A, combat-core) and the week-12 balance pass revises it here.",
  "crit_roll_note": "Golden cases use CRIT_CHANCE exactly 0.0 (never crit) or 1.0 (always crit, randf() in [0,1)), or force_crit (Mark) — so expectations are RNG-independent. In-between chances are covered by a seeded band test in test_damage.gd.",
